From d467a716a292bb3340d36785e897c6a587e12302 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:46:32 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 086/104] render: shape objects draw their effect straight into
 the scene

A `"shape": "quad"` object (upstream logged it as an unsupported VolumeLight) is, in
wallpaper64.exe 2.8.485, its own class (vtable 0x1404d36e8, built by the object factory's
`shape` branch): a square of the scene's orthographic height (GH 0x140285b40), its corners
the first effect's point0..point3 (uv = the point, WE's two triangles 0 2 1 / 0 3 2;
GH 0x1402861b0, the plain quad without them), every pass compiled with DIRECTDRAW 1
(GH 0x140285f40), and the last effect's passes drawn into the scene with the layer's
transform (GH 0x140285b70), the last one additively (GH 0x1402866d0 sets the pass's
blending to 2 = additive). The stock lightshafts effect is the one that uses it
(3319542538's "Rayons lumineux").

CImage builds such an image with no base pass and no colour-blend or tint pass, 1 x 1
composites, and a 6-vertex quad recomputed per frame from the layer's scene rectangle.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "F2 result" (3319542538, health: unsupported VolumeLight)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
